	'k2b323426' => 'What Comes with Every Stay',
	'k2db19639' => 'Private rooms',
	'k2db78696' => 'Our hostel is situated at 14 Quay Lane in the quiet Harbour Ward district. From the central railway station, board the tram directly to the Harbour Ward stop, which sits just a four-minute walk from our front door. Turn right off the tram platform, follow the brick lane toward the water, and look for our wooden doorway and glass entrance framed with potted plants.',
	'k2dfadf9d' => 'The minimum age to stay in our shared dormitory rooms is eighteen years old. Guests under eighteen years of age are welcome to stay at Fumoto Hostel only when accompanied by an adult parent or guardian and accommodated in our private rooms, either the twin or double en-suite. This arrangement helps us preserve a calm, restful, and quiet atmosphere across all shared sleeping quarters.',
	'k2f50341e' => 'The Kitchen &amp; Lounge',
	'k2f9a4e45' => 'A Calm House in Harbour Ward',
	'k306071d6' => '15:00 Check-in and Settling In',
	'k3114dbeb' => 'What are your quiet hours and how are they maintained?',
	'k31d0ff0a' => 'Afternoon',
	'k32e64246' => 'Our shared rooms are designed for quiet rest after a long day in the city. The six-bed mixed dormitory is priced at €29 per night, while the four-bed female dormitory is available at €34 per night. Both options include crisp bed linen, a bath towel, and a secure personal locker free of charge. Each bunk features an individual reading lamp, a power socket, and a bedside wooden shelf for your essentials. Mattresses are chosen for firmness and comfort, and windows open to natural daylight and morning air.',
	'k33fa00a6' => 'Kitchen',
	'k34bbb5b2' => 'Our basement self-service laundry facility is equipped with dependable washing machines and tumble dryers, available for €4 per wash cycle. Gentle laundry detergent is provided with every wash token purchased at the front desk. The laundry space is open daily from 07:00 to 23:00, allowing you to clean and dry your travel clothing conveniently without having to leave the building.',
	'k358def0b' => 'What is the minimum age to stay at Fumoto Hostel?',
	'k37cdd8bf' => 'The house',
	'k3864a8f6' => 'By 19:00, the smell of warm food fills the common room. On Wednesday evenings, Lucía gathers guests around the long oak table for our communal shared supper, while on other nights guests cook side by side using the kitchen. Afterward, travellers drift toward the lounge with books or cups of herbal tea, sharing route notes and train schedules until the room quiets down.',
	'k3b4017c6' => 'Lucía Ferro',
	'k3d55df02' => 'Just three minutes on foot from 14 Quay Lane lies the neighbourhood market. Open daily from early morning, its stalls sell fresh sourdough loaves, seasonal fruit, regional cheeses, and vegetables ideal for cooking in our communal kitchen. Small independent grocers and a neighbourhood bakery line the adjacent brick alleyways, offering warm pastries and fair coffee for early risers setting out into town.',
	'k3de8ddfa' => 'The guest kitchen is open daily from 07:00 to 23:00. It features cooktops, refrigerators, prep tables, cookware, and shared dishware for preparing your own meals during your stay. An optional breakfast is served every morning from 07:00 for €7, including fresh bread, fruit, and hot coffee or tea. Filtered drinking water and warm herbal tea are available in the kitchen throughout the day.',
	'k3f52bd58' => 'Arrival and Confirmation Details',
	'k3f6410e0' => 'Payment is taken directly at the front desk when you check in and collect your room key. We do not require advance payments, card pre-authorisations, or online booking deposits when submitting your reservation enquiry form. At the reception desk, we accept debit cards, major credit cards, and cash payments. There are never any unexpected booking commissions or transaction surcharges added to your stay.',
	'k3fe04b7f' => 'Neighbourhood',
